{"name":"Hay Day","hex":"#dacd81","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hay day","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Eggcorn of heyday."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hay_day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hay Day","blocks":[{"text":"Hay Day is a free-to-play mobile farming simulation game developed and published by Supercell. Hay Day was released for iOS on 21 June 2012 and Android on 20 November 2013. According to a 2013 report, Supercell earned $30 million a month from Hay Day and Clash of Clans. In 2013, Hay Day was the fourth-highest game in revenue generated, with a total of over 1.2 billion dollars in gross income by the end of 2013."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/Hay_Day_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hay_Day","wikidata":"Q15984270"},{"title":"Hay","blocks":[{"text":"Hay is grass, legumes, or other herbaceous plants that have been cut and dried to be stored for use as animal fodder, either for large grazing animals raised as livestock, such as cattle, horses, goats, and sheep, or for smaller domesticated animals such as rabbits and guinea pigs. Pigs can eat hay, but they do not digest it as efficiently as herbivores do."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Roundbale1.jpg/330px-Roundbale1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hay","wikidata":"Q336989"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Hayfield2.jpg/500px-Hayfield2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Hayfield2.jpg/500px-Hayfield2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHayfield2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bales_from_corn_stems_01.jpg/500px-Bales_from_corn_stems_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bales_from_corn_stems_01.jpg/1280px-Bales_from_corn_stems_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bales_from_corn_stems_01.jpg/500px-Bales_from_corn_stems_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baled cornstalks[3]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABales_from_corn_stems_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/LPCC-548-Fenc_de_civada.jpg/500px-LPCC-548-Fenc_de_civada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/LPCC-548-Fenc_de_civada.jpg/1280px-LPCC-548-Fenc_de_civada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/LPCC-548-Fenc_de_civada.jpg/500px-LPCC-548-Fenc_de_civada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Good-quality hay is green and not too coarse and includes plant heads, leaves, and stems.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALPCC-548-Fenc_de_civada.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Round_hay_bale%2C_partially_eaten.jpg/500px-Round_hay_bale%2C_partially_eaten.jpg?ut